// ============================================================================
//  mod_bo1guns.zone  -  the four Black Ops 1 guns, v2.15.0
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  User directive 2026-09-09: *"this mod has a bunch of weapon ports from bo1
//  that i want you to port into my mod ... the m60 lmg, the l96, the browning
//  pistol, the rpg-7"*, from the zm_refreshed build they supplied.
//
//  NAMED EXCEPTION TO HARD RULE 7 (no importing from other mods, zm_refreshed
//  named explicitly). Given by the rule's author, for these four guns only.
//
//  SOURCE: zone_source\refreshed_donor\mod.ff - see how_this_was_built.zone.txt
//  beside it for the exact Linker command and why the whole 23 MB mod.ff is not
//  --load'ed instead. The donor is --load'ed LAST in build_ff.bat, so first-load-
//  wins means it can only supply names nothing above it offers; the ERROR_CATALOGUE
//  section 38 contents-swap trap is impossible from the last slot.
//
//  HOW THIS LIST WAS DERIVED - not typed. Every \key\value\ pair of the eight
//  defs (m60, t5_l96a1, browninghp, rpg - base and upgraded) was parsed, each
//  referenced name classified by its key, and each name checked against all six
//  map fastfiles, the four always-loaded zones (common_zm, patch_zm,
//  code_post_gfx_zm, ui_zm) and mod_base.zone. What that answered:
//
//    121 names exist ONLY in the donor            -> declared below
//      3 fx exist in retail but NOT on every map  -> declared below, so every
//                                                    map has them (they resolve
//                                                    from the retail --loads by
//                                                    first-load-wins, and mod.ff
//                                                    then carries them everywhere)
//     20 need nothing: already in mod.ff (t6_wpn_projectile_rpg7, the two
//        tracers, reticle_side_small, hud_mp_firerate_bolt, reticle_flechette)
//        or in an always-loaded zone or in every map's own ff (the 12 muzzle
//        flashes and the pistol/rifle shell ejects).
//
//  NOTE: `adsOverlayReticle crosshair` on both L96 defs is an ENUM, not a material -
//  stock's own dsr50_zm carries the same value. Nothing to ship for it.
//
//  THE WEAPON DEFS ARE NOT DECLARED HERE. The Linker never reads a raw weapon
//  file, and a declared one would be copied verbatim out of the donor with the
//  refreshed mod's own balance. They ship RAW in weapons\zm\ (trimmed under the
//  20,480 B loader ceiling), which is the mechanism all 14 ported guns use.
// ============================================================================

// --- view / world / projectile models -------------------------------------
xmodel,t6_wpn_launch_rpg7_stow
xmodel,t6_wpn_launch_rpg7_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_launch_rpg7_view_rocket
xmodel,t6_wpn_launch_rpg7_world
xmodel,t6_wpn_lmg_m60_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_lmg_m60_world
xmodel,t6_wpn_pistol_browninghp_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_pistol_browninghp_world
xmodel,vm_t5_l96a1
xmodel,wm_t5_l96a1
xmodel,wm_t5_l96a1_mag

// --- HUD icons and the L96 scope overlay ----------------------------------
material,hud_icon_rpg
material,hud_t5_l96a1
material,menu_mp_weapons_browning
material,menu_mp_weapons_m60
material,mtl_t5_l96a1_scope_overlay

// --- Pack-a-Punch camo, one per gun ---------------------------------------
//
//  🛑 v2.15.4 - camo_m60 IS NOW A RAW FILE IN zone_assets\camo\, AND THE
//  DONOR'S COPY IS DELIBERATELY OVERRIDDEN. The Pack-a-Punched M60 came out with
//  no camo at all (user screenshot, Tunnel survival, 2026-09-09).
//
//  🌟 MEASURED, by dumping every camo asset out of the built mod.ff: of the
//  128 tables the mod owns, 127 carry 12-15 camoMaterials slots and camo_m60
//  carried FOUR. Zombies reads exactly two of those slots - slot 3 is the static
//  Pack-a-Punch camo (-> mc/mtl_weapon_camo_zombies) and slot 8 the animated one
//  (-> mc/mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2*, index 44). In the donor's table slot 3 had
//  an EMPTY materialOverrides list and slot 8 did not exist, so both were dead.
//  This is the same failure the seven Green Run guns had in v2.9.15 - a table too
//  short to hold slot 8 - and it is fixed the same way, with a raw JSON, because
//  CLAUDE.md's measured precedence table says a raw zone_assets\camo\ file beats
//  every --load.
//
//  📝 WHY IT IS SYNTHESISED AND NOT COPIED. The other route - lift a richer
//  copy of the same gun's table out of another fastfile - does not exist here:
//  retail Black Ops 2 has no M60, so no 13-slot camo_m60 exists anywhere
//  (checked across the retail_lists dumps). The template is camo_rpd, the
//  closest structural analogue in the game: also an LMG, also exactly three
//  camo-capable materials, 13 slots. Its three base materials are renamed to the
//  M60's, which were read off the model itself rather than assumed - the GLB for
//  t6_wpn_lmg_m60_view/_world names mtl_t6_wpn_lmg_m60_camo1 / _camo2 / _camo3.
//  Every one of the 13 camoMaterial targets it points at is already owned by
//  mod.ff, so nothing new had to be linked.
//
//  📝 NO camo_qol_m60 COPY IS NEEDED. The seven guns that needed one
//  (mod_locations.zone, v2.11.0) did so because a MAP owned a table of the same
//  name and shadowed mod.ff's. "camo_m60" is defined in no retail fastfile at
//  all, so there is nothing that can shadow it on any map.
camo,camo_browninghp
camo,camo_m60
camo,camo_rpg
camo,camo_t5_l96a1

